Naga Codex Cyber Security — Attribution & Provenance
====================================================

This project is original Naga Codex work (MIT) — a defensive consulting skill pack for authorized security engagements. It synthesizes industry
best practices and is informed by the design patterns of open-source
agent-skill projects. No third-party skill bodies were copied wholesale.

Influential open projects (study / pattern inspiration only):
- mukul975/Anthropic-Cybersecurity-Skills (Apache-2.0) — multi-framework mapping, progressive disclosure
- OWASP/secure-agent-playbook (CC-BY-4.0) — play structure, CWE/OpenCRE-style findings
- UnitOneAI/SecuritySkills (MIT) — normalized finding envelope ideas, framework grounding
- olanokhin/agent-security-skill — OWASP LLM 2025 + Agentic 2026 layered check model
- agentskills.io — open Agent Skills specification

Frameworks referenced (public standards, not proprietary content):
- MITRE ATT&CK, MITRE ATLAS, MITRE D3FEND
- NIST CSF 2.0, NIST AI RMF 1.0, NIST SP 800-61
- OWASP Top 10, OWASP API Top 10, OWASP ASVS, OWASP LLM Top 10 2025, OWASP Agentic Top 10 2026
- CWE, GDPR, NIS2, ISO/IEC 27001:2022, BSI IT-Grundschutz (mapping guidance)

